# SimpleFit Mobile environment variables.
#
# Copy to .env.local for local development (.env.local is git-ignored):
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# RULES
# * EXPO_PUBLIC_* variables are inlined into the JavaScript bundle at build
#   time and can be extracted from the app binary by anyone. They are PUBLIC.
#   Never put secrets, API keys with privileges, or tokens in them.
# * Secrets never live in the app. Anything sensitive at runtime (auth tokens)
#   is obtained from the backend and stored with SecureStore.
# * Restart `pnpm start --clear` after changing values (they are inlined).
# * Document every new variable in this file with a safe placeholder value.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public (bundled into the app)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Base URL of the SimpleFit API (Phoenix backend), no trailing slash.
#
# "localhost" means the device itself, not necessarily your computer:
# * iOS Simulator:     http://localhost:4000 works (shares the Mac's network).
# * Android Emulator:  use http://10.0.2.2:4000 (the emulator's alias for the host).
# * Physical device:   use your computer's LAN IP, e.g. http://192.168.1.20:4000,
#                      with the phone on the same network and the API listening
#                      on 0.0.0.0. Production must use https://.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000

# The web app's origin (SF-37), public. The Sponsor / Brand choice on O05
# continues to the web partner application there (/partners/apply). Leave
# empty and the app says that hand-off is unavailable. https in production.
EXPO_PUBLIC_WEB_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Google sign-in (SF-22). OAuth client IDs are public (they ship in the app);
# a Google client secret is never used and must not be added anywhere.
# Every ID below must also be listed in the API's GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_IDS.
#
# Web application client: the audience of the Google ID tokens the app gets on
# iOS and Android. Required for Google sign-in.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=
# iOS client (bundle ID com.simplefit.boxing). Required on iOS; also becomes
# the iOS URL scheme in app.config.ts, so changing it needs a native rebuild.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=
# Android client (package com.simplefit.boxing + signing certificate SHA-1).
# Reference only: Google matches Android by package and SHA-1, the app does
# not read this value. Each signing key (debug.keystore, EAS, Play App
# Signing) needs its own Android client; a mismatch gives DEVELOPER_ERROR.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID=
